          "name": "godspeed",
          "status": "offered",
          "style": ">",
          "declared_name": "godspeed",
          "name_matches_folder": true,
          "description_chars": 389,
          "source_description": "Godspeed posture — name the axes, iterate cheap in parallel, keep moves that improve any axis and harm none, and don't aim (let the frontier walk itself). Stops clarifying questions and verbose planning in favor of large concurrent tool-call batches. Use for any task framed with godspeed. Triggers: \"godspeed\", \"--with godspeed\", \"/skill:godspeed\", or a task marked with godspeed framing.\n",
          "cache": "hit",
          "rendered_chars": 390,
          "rendered": null
        },
        {
          "name": "omarchy",
          "status": "offered",
          "style": ">",
          "declared_name": "omarchy",
          "name_matches_folder": true,
          "description_chars": 658,
          "source_description": "REQUIRED for end-user customization of Linux desktop, window manager, or system config. Use when editing ~/.config/hypr/, ~/.config/waybar/, ~/.config/walker/, ~/.config/alacritty/, ~/.config/foot/, ~/.config/kitty/, ~/.config/ghostty/, ~/.config/mako/, or ~/.config/omarchy/. Triggers: Hyprland, window rules, animations, keybindings, monitors, gaps, borders, blur, opacity, waybar, walker, terminal config, themes, wallpaper, night light, idle, lock screen, screenshots, reminders, layer rules, workspace settings, display config, and user-facing omarchy commands. Excludes Omarchy source development in ~/.local/share/omarchy/ and `omarchy dev` workflows.\n",
          "cache": "hit",
          "rendered_chars": 659,
          "rendered": null
        },
        {
          "name": "reverse-engineer-anything",
          "status": "offered",
          "style": "plain",
          "declared_name": "reverse-engineer-anything",
          "name_matches_folder": true,
          "description_chars": 300,
          "source_description": "Reverse engineer native, managed, Electron/JavaScript, packaged, firmware, and browser targets with REA. Use shipped-artifact or requested runtime evidence to explain features, compare versions, decompile code, or guide a reconstruction. Skip REA for ordinary source-repository architecture analysis.",
          "cache": "hit",
          "rendered_chars": 300,
          "rendered": null
        },
        {
          "name": "shokunin",
          "status": "offered",
          "style": ">",
          "declared_name": "shokunin",
          "name_matches_folder": true,
          "description_chars": 415,
          "source_description": "Shokunin (職人) — mint domain-specialist agents and train them on a continual learning path (curation, quality gating, understanding, expanding perspective) on OMP and Devin CLI. Thin host binding over the canonical kimi-shokunin protocol. Triggers: \"shokunin\", \"mint a specialist\", \"craft round\", \"train <id>\", \"teach <id>\". Anti-trigger: general orchestration and any-problem planning are tower/ufo, not this skill.\n",
          "cache": "hit",
          "rendered_chars": 416,
          "rendered": null
        },
        {
          "name": "swarm",
          "status": "offered",
          "style": ">",
          "declared_name": "swarm",
          "name_matches_folder": true,
          "description_chars": 334,
          "source_description": "Kimi-style swarm toggle and bounded parallel task waves for OMP and Devin CLI. Uses the repository wave validator, one batched dispatch per wave (an OMP task call, or one same-response run_subagent batch on Devin), and the host's configured routing; never mutates routing configuration or turns child tasks into UFO Sighting missions.\n",
          "cache": "hit",
          "rendered_chars": 335,
          "rendered": null
        },
        {
          "name": "tower",
          "status": "offered",
          "style": ">",
          "declared_name": "tower",
          "name_matches_folder": true,
          "description_chars": 358,
          "source_description": "Experimental worktree orchestration for OMP and Devin CLI. Use /tower to plan and coordinate independent work in real, separate Git worktrees, then integrate and verify from one parent session. Dispatched workers run under the Godspeed posture; UFO Sighting stays an operator display surface for deliberately registered missions, never a second orchestrator.\n",
          "cache": "hit",
          "rendered_chars": 359,
          "rendered": null
        },
        {
          "name": "ufo",
          "status": "offered",
          "style": ">",
          "declared_name": "ufo",
          "name_matches_folder": true,
          "description_chars": 426,
          "source_description": "UFO-FSD operator and mission surface for OMP and Devin CLI — open the sighting wall, steer and read live missions, launch fleets and native trials, and run routed work on the global OMP cascade table. Typing \"ufo\" or \"/ufo\" from any directory activates it; \"open the hatch\", \"open ufo sighting\", and \"i wanna see the ufos\" open the wall immediately. Outside the ufo-fsd-alpha checkout it degrades to advisory mode and says so.\n",
          "cache": "hit",
